Quoted import names containing `}` can make ordinary linting panic while computing a fix, even without `--fix`:

```ts
import type { "}" as A } from 'm';
import { B, C } from 'm';
type T = A | B;
C();
```

Search for the closing brace after the last named specifier and before the module source, validating the search bounds before slicing. Add regressions for ordinary linting and autofixes covering quoted names, comments, trailing commas, empty lists, and both import orders. The fixed output matches typescript-eslint.

A single-use member read was never inlined into a call because the call guard skipped any call whose callee was an identifier. The guard now only blocks the case where the replaced variable is the callee, since inlining it there would change `this`.

## Call arguments

```js
// Before
function getTexture(cubemaps, texture, mapTextureMapping) {
  var cubemap = cubemaps.get(texture).texture;
  return mapTextureMapping(cubemap, texture.mapping);
}

// After
function getTexture(cubemaps, texture, mapTextureMapping) {
  return mapTextureMapping(cubemaps.get(texture).texture, texture.mapping);
}
```

## Call callees

This case is unchanged because `o.method()` would call `method` with `this` set to `o`:

```js
function call(o) {
  var method = o.method;
  return method();
}
```

`typescript.js` shrinks by 1,827 B, or 459 B gzipped.

`new` does not take `this` from a member reference, so the `this` guard on `new` expressions is removed. Single-use member reads can now be inlined into both the constructor and its arguments.

## Constructor

```js
// Before
function create(o) {
  var Ctor = o.Ctor;
  return new Ctor(o.options);
}

// After
function create(o) {
  return new o.Ctor(o.options);
}
```

## Arguments

```js
// Before
function create(o, Ctor) {
  var options = o.options;
  return new Ctor(options);
}

// After
function create(o, Ctor) {
  return new Ctor(o.options);
}
```

A single-use member read is now inlined into a call callee as `(0, o.m)()`, so `m` still runs without `this` bound to `o`. This matches terser, uglify-js and swc. esbuild keeps the variable, so the affected esbuild-derived expectations now have a note.

The tagged-template path already used this rewrite; both paths now share `passes_this_when_called`.

## Member callees

```js
// Before
function call(o) {
  var method = o.method;
  return method(o.value);
}

// After
function call(o) {
  return (0, o.method)(o.value);
}
```

## Optional member callees

```js
// Before
function call(o) {
  var method = o?.method;
  return method();
}

// After
function call(o) {
  return (0, o?.method)();
}
```

When two adjacent cases have the same body and that body always exits the switch (`return`, `throw`, `break` or `continue`), the earlier body is emptied so it falls through to the later one.

```js
// Input
export function isConstraint(node, parent) {
  switch (node.kind) {
    case 165: return node === parent.constraint;
    case 347: return node === parent.constraint;
    case 1: visit(node); break;
    case 2: visit(node); break;
    default: return false;
  }
}
export function minValue(kind) {
  switch (kind) {
    case 208:
    case 209: return -2147483648;
    default: return -2147483648;
  }
}
```

Before:

```js
export function isConstraint(node, parent) {
	switch (node.kind) {
		case 165: return node === parent.constraint;
		case 347: return node === parent.constraint;
		case 1:
			visit(node);
			break;
		case 2:
			visit(node);
			break;
		default: return !1;
	}
}
export function minValue(kind) {
	switch (kind) {
		case 208:
		case 209: return -2147483648;
		default: return -2147483648;
	}
}
```

After:

```js
export function isConstraint(node, parent) {
	switch (node.kind) {
		case 165:
		case 347: return node === parent.constraint;
		case 1:
		case 2:
			visit(node);
			break;
		default: return !1;
	}
}
export function minValue(kind) {
	return -2147483648;
}
```

- When the later body is the last one in the switch, a trailing unlabeled `break` is ignored on both sides, because falling off the end also exits the switch. The merge runs before `try_fold_switch` remo
